title: Physics Equations
subject: Physics
level: GCSE
emoji: 📐
description: The key equations you need to memorise, with units.
---
Density formula? :: Density (kg/m³) = mass ÷ volume
Moment of a force? :: Moment (Nm) = force × perpendicular distance from pivot
Work done? :: Work done (J) = force × distance moved
Power in terms of work done? :: Power (W) = work done ÷ time
Change in thermal energy? :: ΔE = m × c × Δθ (specific heat capacity)
Energy for a change of state? :: E = m × L (specific latent heat)
Potential difference in terms of energy and charge? :: V = E ÷ Q
Transformer equation? :: Vp ÷ Vs = Np ÷ Ns
Force on a conductor in a magnetic field? :: F = B × I × l
Wave period? :: T = 1 ÷ f
Average speed? :: v = s ÷ t
Equation of motion that does not involve time? :: v² = u² + 2as
Force in terms of change in momentum? :: F = (mv − mu) ÷ t
What is needed for an object to move in a circle? :: A resultant force towards the centre of the circle.
Specific heat capacity definition? :: The energy needed to raise the temperature of 1 kg of a substance by 1 °C.
Unit of specific heat capacity? :: J/kg°C
Unit of energy? :: Joule (J)
Unit of force? :: Newton (N)
Unit of pressure? :: Pascal (Pa) or N/m²
